      "content": "It is incredibly painful to feel like your identity is tied to external validation, but the idea that your entire self is ruined because one expectation has shifted is a severe overestimation of your worth. That \"stain\" is simply the end of a role, not the end of you; you are still capable of change and redefining yourself, even if it feels impossible now. You don't have to \"fix\" anything; you can simply allow yourself the grace to explore who you are outside of that perfect mold.",
